    {
      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "ヤギのミルクを飲んだり、ヤギの肉を食べたり、ヤギの毛皮で服を作ったり、ヤギの糞を土に混ぜて野菜を作ったりすることができます。",
      "english_translation": "You can drink goat's milk, eat goat meat, make clothes from goat hair, and grow vegetables by mixing goat manure with soil."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "最近、地球の環境を守るために、ヤギの新しい使い方が始まっています。",
      "english_translation": "Recently, new uses for goats have begun as a way to protect the Earth's environment."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "屋上に緑を増やす研究のためです。",
      "english_translation": "This is for research on increasing greenery on rooftops."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "そして、2018年から、1年のうち数日だけ、屋上のいらない草をヤギに食べてもらうヤギ除草を始めました。",
      "english_translation": "Furthermore, starting in 2018, we began using goats to clear unwanted grass from our rooftops, feeding them only for a few days each year."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "人が機械を使っていらない草を取ると、大きな音や二酸化炭素（CO2）が出ます。",
      "english_translation": "When people use machines to remove weeds, it produces a lot of noise and carbon dioxide (CO2)."
    }
  ],
